From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:14:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dwc2d: several keyboards, mice and gamepads at once (#450)

Each input function polls on a host channel of its own, taken from a
pool of channels 3 to 7 (0 does control transfers, the network
adapters use 1 and 2). Up to five functions run at once; a further one
is logged and left out until another one goes. Removing a device frees
the channels of all its functions.

mouse::find returns every pointer and gamepad interface of a device,
not only the first, and the device is configured once. Gamepads get
controller ids 0, 1, ... in plug order, and a freed id is given again.

The pool sits in inputs.rs, apart from the HID code, so that the usb
scheme can take its channels from it later.
